{%- doc -%}
  Renders `true` when a whole option — the label and every one of its values — must be kept off
  the storefront, and nothing otherwise.

  Driven by `product.metafields.custom.hidden_options`, a list of option names:

    ["Size"]

  Names are matched ignoring case and spaces, the same way `hidden_variants` entries are.

  This is the blunt version of `variant-hidden`: that one takes single values out of a picker and
  leaves the option in place, this one takes the option away entirely. The variant is still chosen
  — the picker keeps the selected value in a hidden input so the option still resolves and the
  product stays buyable — the customer just has no say in it, so an option is only worth hiding
  when every one of its values would do.

  @param {object} product_resource - The product the option belongs to.
  @param {object} product_option - The option to test, as returned by `options_with_values`.

  @example
  {% capture option_hidden %}
    {% render 'variant-option-hidden', product_resource: product_resource, product_option: product_option %}
  {% endcapture %}
  {% if option_hidden != blank %}
    ...
  {% endif %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign is_hidden = false
  assign hidden_options = product_resource.metafields.custom.hidden_options.value

  if hidden_options != blank
    assign option_key = product_option.name | downcase | replace: ' ', ''

    for hidden_entry in hidden_options
      assign hidden_key = hidden_entry | append: '' | downcase | replace: ' ', ''
      if hidden_key != blank and hidden_key == option_key
        assign is_hidden = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{%- if is_hidden -%}true{%- endif -%}
